  "prefLabel": "Bea 502.50 Subdivision",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Bea 502.50 “Subdivision” means “subdivision” as defined in RSA 672:14, namely, “the division of the lot, tract, or parcel of land into 2 or more lots, plats, sites, or other division of land for the purpose, whether immediate or future, of sale, rent, lease, condominium conveyance, or building development. It includes re-subdivision and, when appropriate to the context, related to the process of subdividing or to the land or territory subdivided.”\n\nSource. #14043, eff 8-8-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/bea500.html"
